{-
   What a sum's **declaration** refuses - Analysis-IR.md §11.4's G7d, and
   `doc/spec/declarations.md`'s pinned constructor values.

   # resolver: ownership

   A file of its own, because a declaration that reported is a declaration the bodies below it are
   not resolved against: the expression refusals are `Reject.Sum.yana`, and a fixture holding both
   would only ever show the first of the two.
-}

-- Two constructors of one name build two different types, so the name says nothing about which.
data First = Same(I32) | NoFirst
data Second = Same(Bool) | NoSecond

-- Two constructors naming one number. Reported at the later of the two, which is the one whose
-- number can change without renumbering everything after it.
data Collides = @value(2) A | @value(13) B | @value(2) C

-- The same collision without a second attribute, because an unpinned constructor continues from the
-- one before it: `Next` is 3, which `Also` was pinned to.
data Continued = @value(2) FirstOf | Next | @value(3) Also

-- A constructor that carries something. What the value would name is the tag beside the payload
-- rather than the value itself, so there is nothing for it to pin.
data WithPayload = @value(2) Held(I32) | Nothing

-- An argument that is not a whole number written down. The number is one an ABI on the other side
-- of a boundary already fixed, so there is nothing here for an expression to compute.
data NotALiteral = @value(1 + 1) A2 | B2
data NotANumber = @value("two") A3 | B3
data TooMany = @value(1, 2) A4 | B4

-- Every other attribute on a constructor, which this stage reads none of - a constructor is not a
-- declaration with a placement table to report against.
data Unknown = @inline A5 | B5

-- A name twice in one constructor, which would make a projection of it name whichever the lookup
-- reached first. Per constructor rather than per record: two arms of a sum are two shapes over one
-- storage, so `Left {at: I32} | Right {at: Bool}` names one thing in each and the match that
-- reached a projection is what settles which.
data Repeated = Left {at: I32, at: I32} | Right {at: Bool}

fn main() -> I32 = 0
